.TH VIBECODER-ADMIN 1 "2026-11-08" "vibecoder 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vibecoder-admin \- administer a local vibecoder installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibecoder-admin
.RI [ --config " FILE" ]
.RI [ --json ]
.RI { status | doctor | config | projects | accounts | credentials | agents | service | setup }
.SH DESCRIPTION
Provides validated administration without direct JSON or SQLite editing. Mutating
operations require root. Secrets are accepted from an un-echoed TTY or an already
open file descriptor and are never accepted as command arguments.
.PP
.B setup init
provides a resumable first-run wizard. Its non-interactive mode applies only explicit
values and never activates READY unless --activate is supplied.
.PP
.B backup create|list|inspect|verify|restore
manages versioned private backups. Creation and restore require an explicit offline
confirmation, persistent pause and no active leases. Restore always establishes an
operational recovery barrier.
.PP
.B maintenance status|check|reconcile|prepare-upgrade|finish-upgrade
inspects and recovers maintenance state without contacting GitHub or Codex.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vibecoder/supervisor.json
Validated supervisor configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/vibecoder/accounts.json
Non-secret Codex account runtime configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/vibecoder/secrets
Protected credential store.
.SH SECURITY
The service user is not an administrator. Local credential revocation does not revoke
the corresponding token at its remote provider.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vibecoder-supervisor (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
